<title>JAPAN: Biwako Bank - 6mth parent forecast.</title>
<headline>Biwako Bank - 6mth parent forecast.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in billions of yen unless specified)</p>
<p>			   LATEST	    PREVIOUS	   ACTUAL</p>
<p> (Parent)	     FORECAST	   FORECAST	  YEAR-AGO</p>
<p> Revenues	    23.14		23.14		28.73</p>
<p> Operating	    4.65		 4.65		 5.41</p>
<p> Current		1.39		 1.39		 2.56</p>
<p> Net	     loss 1.35	  prft 1.65	   prft 847 million</p>
<p>NOTE - Biwako Bank Ltd is a regional bank based in Shiga prefecture.  </p>
<p>Biwako Bank said in a statement that it would post a parent net loss as it expects special losses of three billion yen stemming from the suspected misuse of bank funds by a former employee.</p>
<p>Biwako said, however, that it will not change its forecast for parent net profit of one billion yen for the 1996/97 financial year ending next March, as it would cover the special loss by selling stocks and by increasing operating profits.</p>
<p>The bank said last week that the suspected fund misappropriation, totalling about 3.4 billion yen, would do only limited damage to its financial health.</p>
</text>
